- `precedence(n2, n3)`: The model sequences checking referee reports and monitoring their completion, but the text states they should happen "At the same time", requiring an AND gateway for concurrency.
- `branch(b1, XOR)`: Missing guard conditions on the outgoing edges to `c1` and `n4` to evaluate whether the referee reports have been completed.
- `branch(b2, XOR)`: The model completely omits the negative conditional path and its required action "flag it again and send another reminder" (and loop back) for when the referee reports are still not completed after re-checking.
- `branch(b2, XOR)`: Missing guard conditions on its outgoing edge(s).
- `branch(b3, XOR)`: Missing guard conditions on the outgoing edges to `n10` and `c2` to evaluate "if a Psychometric Test is required".
- `branch(b4, XOR)`: Missing guard conditions on the outgoing edges to `n11` and `n12` to evaluate "if an HR Specialist is required".
- `precedence(c2, n13)`: The model erroneously converges all paths (including when tests are scheduled) into `n13` ("coordinate second round of selection"), but the text specifies this action only occurs on the specific path where a psychometric test is not required ("If not, you can continue with the process and coordinate the second round of selection").
- `defines(...)`: Variables `v1`, `v2`, `v3`, and `v4` are defined with empty ranges `{}` instead of valid boolean or categorical domains (e.g., true/false) derived from the text.

